From: CoreELEC
Subject: [PATCH] libCEC: preserve the interpretation of a held power toggle

Backport the wake-versus-off classification from upstream commit
efe7d98c891ad26b65f2844c4f7e060476d8cc64 (Pulse-Eight/libcec#744).
An inactive or standby source interprets Power as activation; do not forward
that activation as a shutdown-capable application key.

Deliver Power On callbacks for that interpretation and retain it for the
existing held-key lifetime, scoped to sender, destination and raw key. Expire
it across suspend with CLOCK_BOOTTIME when available, and cancel old key state
on client retirement. Match releases to their power-key sender/destination.
Explicit Power Off, ordinary input and active-source runtime Power remain.
No startup grace period, new worker or public adapter ABI change.

--- a/src/libcec/CECClient.h
